From: Felix <301398501+felixfelix-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 14:11:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(lr2021): configurable FLRC sync word match +
 511-byte payloads

- add setFlrcSyncWordMatch() selecting which FLRC sync words the receiver
  matches (sw_match bits of SET_FLRC_PACKET_PARAMS): Match1 (default,
  stock behavior), Match1+2 or Match1+2+3, with new
  RADIOLIB_LR2021_FLRC_SYNC_MATCH_* constants
- replace all hardcoded syncMatch=0x01 emissions with the cached value so
  re-configuration methods (setPreambleLength/setCRC/setSyncWord) preserve it
- widen fixed/variablePacketLengthMode() to uint16_t and raise the FLRC
  packet length cap to 511 bytes (16-bit payload length field); all other
  modems remain capped at 255
- cache the FLRC payload length so re-configuration preserves it
- run CALIB_FRONT_END (image rejection, freq/4 + HF path bit) during Rx
  staging right after SET_RX_PATH, as required before starting Rx

Validated on host against golden SPI frames captured from the RP2040
range-test firmware (multi_radio_sweep_rx_v4): SET_FLRC_PACKET_PARAMS
{0x0E, 0x7C, 0x01, 0xFF} for Match123 + fixed 511-byte payloads.
