From bca91a6485e84f3cf171e2033ee7b329f8487e7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix <301398501+felixfelix-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 18:09:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(lr2021): pass the cached FLRC sync match when staging
 TX

stageMode(RADIOLIB_RADIO_MODE_TX) re-emits SET_FLRC_PACKET_PARAMS and was the
last call site still passing a hard-coded syncMatch = 0x01 (Match1) instead of
the cached this->flrcSyncMatch. A board configured for Match123 that
transmitted and then returned to RX therefore silently reverted to Match1-only
reception - the cross-board FLRC breakage mode.

Behavior-invariant for stock RadioLib: flrcSyncMatch defaults to
RADIOLIB_LR2021_FLRC_SYNC_MATCH_1 (0x01), so a radio that never calls
setFlrcSyncWordMatch() emits exactly the same byte1 as before.

Pinned by the host test check 4 in
tests/src/lr2021_flrc_match123/test_lr2021_flrc_match123.cpp, which asserts
every SET_FLRC_PACKET_PARAMS emitted from transmit() carries the cached match
(golden 0E 7C 01 FF); RED before this commit emitted 0E 4C 01 FF.
---
 src/modules/LR2021/LR2021.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

